          "payload": {
            "iss": "https://api.example",
            "dwk": "aauth-resource.json",
            "aud": "https://ps.example",
            "jti": "ec12c052-ab17-49e1-88d3-5e2317ba82c4",
            "ps": "https://ps.example",
            "sub": "8f14e45fceea167a5a36dedd4bea2543",
            "person_token_jti": "pt-32d653",
            "agent_jkt": "tcP75aIbpvVmzZ0P-LIZeoLua8SuE8RGM4tO_2OkRpg",
            "scope": "documents.write",
            "iat": 1776222954,
            "exp": 1776223254
          },
          "signature_b64": "6QznE3sOp9JX6RY4a0olsuHZSIKAn5t4HwyxK9M8fOOIW9D2nQGR18uObb97Ui6BZdb0F8gTP7BqI5BO0WRsDA"
        }
      ],
      "signature": {
        "scheme": "jwt",
        "signature_base": "\"@method\": POST\n\"@authority\": api.example\n\"@path\": /documents\n\"signature-key\": sig=jwt;jwt=\"eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSIsImtpZCI6InBzLWtleS0xIiwidHlwIjoiYWEtcGVyc29uK2p3dCJ9…\"\n\"@signature-params\": (\"@method\" \"@authority\" \"@path\" \"signature-key\");created=1700000120;alg=\"ed25519\"",
        "signature_input": "sig=(\"@method\" \"@authority\" \"@path\" \"signature-key\");created=1700000120;alg=\"ed25519\"",
        "signature_key": "sig=jwt;jwt=\"eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSIsImtpZCI6InBzLWtleS0xIiwidHlwIjoiYWEtcGVyc29uK2p3dCJ9…\"",
        "covered_components": [
          "@method",
          "@authority",
          "@path",
          "signature-key"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": [
        "Identity was enough for GET /me. Writing a document is not, so the resource challenges here with requirement=auth-token while continuing to serve the rest on the person token.",
        "The resource MUST have verified a person token before it issues a resource token. That is what makes the identity in the resource token PS-asserted rather than agent-asserted.",
        "ps, sub and person_token_jti are copied out of the person token it just verified. agent_jkt binds the resource token to the agent's key.",
        "No agent identifier appears in the resource token. agent_jkt and cnf are the binding; the PS learns the agent's identity from the agent token that signs the request to it.",
        "person_token_jti is what makes mission stripping detectable: the PS resolves the exact person token it issued and rejects any mismatch in ps, sub, mission_s256 or tenant.",
        "From here the flow continues as PS authorization access — the agent sends the resource token to its PS's auth_token_endpoint."
      ],
      "is_response": false
    }
  ]
}
